/*
🔹 Intuition (step-by-step)

If total cards isn’t divisible by groupSize, grouping is impossible.

Sort the hand so we always process smallest values first.

Use a frequency map to track unused cards.

When we see a card num that still has count:

It must start a group (no smaller card can absorb it).

Try to build a consecutive group:

Consume one card from num, num+1, ..., num+groupSize-1

If any card is missing → impossible.

Each card is used exactly once.



🔹 Time Complexity

O(n log n) due to sorting

Greedy grouping itself is O(n) (each card is consumed once)

🔹 Space Complexity

O(n) for the frequency map


*/
class Solution {
    public boolean isNStraightHand(int[] hand, int groupSize) {
        if(hand.length % groupSize !=0 )return false;
        Arrays.sort(hand);
        Map<Integer,Integer> count = new HashMap<>();
        for(int i:hand){
            count.put(i,count.getOrDefault(i,0)+1);
        }
        for(int i:hand){
            if(count.get(i)==0)continue;
            for(int j=i;j<i+groupSize;j++){
                if(count.getOrDefault(j,0) == 0)return false;
                count.put(j,count.get(j)-1);
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
}
